Package: streamfind
Title: DuckDB-Backed Project Framework for Analytical Workflows
Version: 1.0.0
Author: Ricardo Cunha [cre, aut, fnd] (<https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6791-0119>)
Maintainer: Ricardo Cunha <cunha@iuta.de>
Authors@R: c(
        person("Ricardo", "Cunha", email="cunha@iuta.de", role=c("cre", "aut", "fnd"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6791-0119")),
        person("Walter", "Laurito", email="laurito@fzi.de", role = "ctb")
    )
Description: streamfind provides a DuckDB-backed project framework for
    assembling, running, and inspecting analytical workflows in R. The
    current package centres on Project child classes that expose
    domain-specific interfaces for mass spectrometry and non-target
    analysis, including ProjectMassSpec, ProjectMassSpecSpectra,
    ProjectMassSpecChromatograms, and ProjectNonTargetAnalysis.
    Workflows are expressed as ordered Method objects, persisted with the
    project, executed reproducibly, and inspected through both
    programmatic APIs and an integrated Shiny application. streamfind is
    developed within the project "Flexible Data Analysis and Workflow
    Designer to Identify Chemicals in the Water Cycle" and is intended
    to support transparent, reusable processing pipelines for research
    and routine analytical work.
